{
  "title": "Dependencies",
  "description": "crates.io is the Rust community’s central package registry that serves as a location to discover and download packages. cargo is configured to use it by default to find requested packages.",
  "body": {
    "type": "document",
    "children": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 1,
        "id": "dependencies",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Dependencies"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "link",
            "href": "https://crates.io/",
            "title": null,
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "crates.io"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " is the Rust community’s central "
          },
          {
            "type": "link",
            "href": "https://corpus.test/appendix/glossary.html#package-registry",
            "title": "\"package-registry\" (glossary entry)",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "emphasis",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": "package registry"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " that serves as a location to discover and download "
          },
          {
            "type": "link",
            "href": "https://corpus.test/appendix/glossary.html#package",
            "title": "\"package\" (glossary entry)",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "packages"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": ". "
          },
          {
            "type": "inline_code",
            "code": "cargo"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " is configured to use it by default to find requested packages."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "To depend on a library hosted on "
          },
          {
            "type": "link",
            "href": "https://crates.io/",
            "title": null,
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "crates.io"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": ", add it to your "
          },
          {
            "type": "inline_code",
            "code": "Cargo.toml"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "id": "adding-a-dependency",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Adding a dependency"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "If your "
          },
          {
            "type": "inline_code",
            "code": "Cargo.toml"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " doesn’t already have a "
          },
          {
            "type": "inline_code",
            "code": "[dependencies]"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " section, add that, then list the "
          },
          {
            "type": "link",
            "href": "https://corpus.test/appendix/glossary.html#crate",
            "title": "\"crate\" (glossary entry)",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "crate"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " name and version that you would like to use. This example adds a dependency on the "
          },
          {
            "type": "inline_code",
            "code": "time"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " crate:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "code_block",
        "language": "toml",
        "code": "[dependencies]\ntime = \"0.1.12\""
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "The version string is a "
          },
          {
            "type": "link",
            "href": "https://semver.org/",
            "title": null,
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "SemVer"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " version requirement. The "
          },
          {
            "type": "link",
            "href": "https://corpus.test/reference/specifying-dependencies.html",
            "title": null,
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "specifying dependencies"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " docs have more information about the options you have here."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "If you also wanted to add a dependency on the "
          },
          {
            "type": "inline_code",
            "code": "regex"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " crate, you would not need to add "
          },
          {
            "type": "inline_code",
            "code": "[dependencies]"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " for each crate listed. Here’s what your whole "
          },
          {
            "type": "inline_code",
            "code": "Cargo.toml"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " file would look like with dependencies on the "
          },
          {
            "type": "inline_code",
            "code": "time"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " and "
          },
          {
            "type": "inline_code",
            "code": "regex"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " crates:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "code_block",
        "language": "toml",
        "code": "[package]\nname = \"hello_world\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nedition = \"2024\"\n\n[dependencies]\ntime = \"0.1.12\"\nregex = \"0.1.41\""
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Re-run "
          },
          {
            "type": "inline_code",
            "code": "cargo build"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": ", and Cargo will fetch the new dependencies and all of their dependencies, compile them all, and update the "
          },
          {
            "type": "inline_code",
            "code": "Cargo.lock"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": ":"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "code_block",
        "language": "bash",
        "code": "$ cargo build\n      Updating crates.io index\n   Downloading memchr v0.1.5\n   Downloading libc v0.1.10\n   Downloading regex-syntax v0.2.1\n   Downloading memchr v0.1.5\n   Downloading aho-corasick v0.3.0\n   Downloading regex v0.1.41\n     Compiling memchr v0.1.5\n     Compiling libc v0.1.10\n     Compiling regex-syntax v0.2.1\n     Compiling memchr v0.1.5\n     Compiling aho-corasick v0.3.0\n     Compiling regex v0.1.41\n     Compiling hello_world v0.1.0 (file:///path/to/package/hello_world)"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "inline_code",
            "code": "Cargo.lock"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " contains the exact information about which revision was used for all of these dependencies."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Now, if "
          },
          {
            "type": "inline_code",
            "code": "regex"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " gets updated, you will still build with the same revision until you choose to run "
          },
          {
            "type": "inline_code",
            "code": "cargo update"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "You can now use the "
          },
          {
            "type": "inline_code",
            "code": "regex"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " library in "
          },
          {
            "type": "inline_code",
            "code": "main.rs"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "code_block",
        "language": "rust",
        "code": "use regex::Regex;\n\nfn main() {\n    let re = Regex::new(r\"^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$\").unwrap();\n    println!(\"Did our date match? {}\", re.is_match(\"2014-01-01\"));\n}"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Running it will show:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "code_block",
        "language": "bash",
        "code": "$ cargo run\n   Running `target/hello_world`\nDid our date match? true"
      }
    ]
  }
}
